BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Walk This Way: 80s 5K & Block Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260912T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260912T220000
DTSTAMP:20260831T153732Z
UID:gz-walk-this-way-80s-5k-block-party-1886398@southbaldwinchamber.com
DESCRIPTION:Description\nLace Up\, Dress Up & Party Like It’s 1985!\nGet
  ready to grab your neon\, tease your hair\, and break out the leg warmers
  because\nWalk This Way: 80’s 5K & Block Party\nis bringing the ultimate
  throwback experience to Downtown Foley!  This high-energy\, 80s-themed e
 vent combines a fun and festive 5K with an unforgettable block party\, all
  while supporting local education initiatives through the South Baldwin Ch
 amber Foundation.\nWhether you’re running\, walking\, skating\, or simpl
 y showing up for the music and nostalgia\, this is your chance to celebrat
 e the decade of mixtapes\, mullets\, and moonwalks in totally tubular styl
 e.\nPURCHASE TICKETS HERE\nThe 80’s 5K\nParticipants will take on a scen
 ic 5K course winding through Historic Downtown Foley and the beautiful Ros
 e Trail before crossing the finish line at Heritage Park.\nCostumes are hi
 ghly encouraged! Dust off your windbreakers\, rock your brightest neon\, c
 hannel your favorite 80s icon\, and bring the energy from start to finish.
 \nWhether you’re chasing a personal best or just cruising with friends\,
  this event is all about having fun and embracing the spirit of the decade
 .\nThe Block Party\nFollowing the race\, Heritage Park transforms into the
  ultimate 80s celebration\, with an epic Block Party featuring a live 80s 
 cover band\, Disco Kiss\, and special guest 80's Condo Queen Kylee Kubat\,
  turning the finish line into a full-scale throwback with music\, dancing
 \, and nonstop fun. Bring your friends\, relive the glory days\, and celeb
 rate under the lights as we turn Heritage Park into a retro party destinat
 ion.\nBYOB Friendly\nParticipants and guests are welcome to bring their ow
 n beverages to enjoy during the block party\, provided they comply with ev
 ent guidelines and local regulations.\nFood will be available for purchase
  from a variety of food truck vendors throughout the evening.\nNot a Runne
 r? Join the Party Anyway!\nWant all the fun without the 5K? Block Party On
 ly Tickets are available for those who want to skip the race and head stra
 ight to the celebration. Because let’s be honest—not everyone wants to
  run\, but everyone deserves a good party.\n\n---\n🌐 View original even
 t: https://businesshub.southbaldwinchamber.com/calendar/Details/walk-this-
 way-80s-5k-block-party-1886398
LOCATION:Foley Heritage Park\, Foley\,\, AL\, 36535\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Mental Health First Aid
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260916T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260916T163000
DTSTAMP:20260831T153732Z
UID:gz-youth-mental-health-first-aid-1905931@southbaldwinchamber.com
DESCRIPTION:Description\n# Youth Mental Health First Aid Training\n\nThe J
 ennifer Claire Moore Foundation is offering **Youth Mental Health First Ai
 d**\, an 8-hour training designed to help adults recognize and respond to 
 mental health and substance use challenges in adolescents. Participants wi
 ll learn about common youth mental health concerns\, adolescent developmen
 t\, and a five-step action plan for supporting young people in both crisis
  and non-crisis situations.\n\n**Training Details:**\n **Wednesday\, Septe
 mber 16\, 2026**\n **8:30 AM–4:30 PM**\n **Bryant Bank – Daphne Commun
 ity Room**\n1801 US Hwy 98\, Daphne\, AL 36526\n **$130 per person** — m
 aterials and lunch included\n**25 spots available**\n\n**The first 10 regi
 strants can save $30 with code YMHFA30.**\n\nThis training is a valuable o
 pportunity for anyone who works with or supports youth to build the knowle
 dge and confidence needed to recognize concerns early and connect young pe
 ople with appropriate support.\n\n---\n🌐 View original event: https://b
 usinesshub.southbaldwinchamber.com/calendar/Details/youth-mental-health-fi
 rst-aid-1905931
LOCATION:Bryant Bank - Daphne Community Room\, 1801 US-98\, Daphne\,\, AL
 \, 36526\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MT Jones at OWA Theater
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260916T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260916T210000
DTSTAMP:20260831T153732Z
UID:gz-mt-jones-at-owa-theater-1776167@southbaldwinchamber.com
DESCRIPTION:Description\nCatch UK soul artist MT Jones live at OWA Theater
  on September 16\, 2026!\nWhile in town for Americana Fest 2026\, MT Jones
  is making a handful of special performances\, and OWA Theater is one of t
 hem! With smooth vocals\, heartfelt lyrics\, and a sound that blends class
 ic soul with a modern edge\, this is your chance to experience an artist o
 n the rise in an intimate live setting.\nDoors open at 6:00 PM.\nAbout MT 
 Jones\nGathering inspiration from 60s and 70s soul greats across the Atlan
 tic to modern R&B and jazz\, MT Jones evokes a sound that is both contempo
 rary and timeless. His deeply soulful vocals transport you straight back t
 o a smoke-filled speak easy which somehow still feels fresh and innovative
 .\nBetween stints working on music regularly in Liverpool & London\, Jones
  has travelled the world as a musician & penned songs for other artists\, 
 making a name for himself as a gifted and prolific songwriter.\nSince then
 \, lockdown gave him the time and space to put his talent under his own na
 me. His debut single ‘I Won't Ever Say Goodbye’ is a soulful\, heart-o
 n-sleeve ballad that marks the start of big things & his latest single ‘
 Feeling Lonely’ has quickly followed suit. He has received great support
  from BBC\, introducing multiple spins on 1xtra\, a ‘Step up’ artist o
 n the show. He has also enjoyed strong playlist support from Spotify inclu
 ding several New Music Friday adds in the UK.\nThis is only the start for 
 this highly memorable and distinctive singer\, song writer\, musician and 
 creator!\nGrab your tickets today!\n\n---\n🌐 View original event: https
 ://businesshub.southbaldwinchamber.com/calendar/Details/mt-jones-at-owa-th
 eater-1776167
LOCATION:OWA Theater\, 205-A N OWA Boulevard\, Foley\,\, AL\, 36535\, Unit
 ed States
END:VEVENT
