 raising vital funds to support local education.\nDesigned for players of a
 ll skill levels\, this event invites teams of two to pick up a paddle and 
 make a difference on and off the court.\nProceeds from the tournament dire
 ctly benefit local education initiatives\, providing resources\, grants\, 
 and opportunities for students and teachers in our community.\nREGISTER NO
 W\nTournament Structure & Divisions\nTo ensure fair\, highly competitive p
 lay\, divisions will be broken down by skill and age.\nSkill Levels\nBegin
 ner\nIntermediate\nAdvanced\nAge Groups\n8–35 | 35–50 | 50–60 | 60
 –69 | 70+\nNote: Players are permitted to play down in an age bracket on
 ly. To ensure playable brackets\, the tournament director reserves the rig
 ht to combine or split age groups if necessary.\nFormat\nGender Doubles (T
 eams of 2)\nRound Robin stage followed by a Playoff bracket.\nDUPR Impact:
  This is a fun\, charity-focused tournament and will not affect your DUPR 
 rating\nRegistration Details\nEntry Fee: $40 per player\nClever Pickleball
  Registration Platform\nImportant Rule: Please register for only one (1) e
