BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overdose Drug Awareness Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260830T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260830T200000
DTSTAMP:20260831T153732Z
UID:gz-overdose-drug-awareness-day-1888662@southbaldwinchamber.com
DESCRIPTION:Description\nOne Big Family\, Driven by Hope.\nJoin Big Fish M
 inistries this International Overdose Awareness Day in Foley\, Alabama\, a
 s we honor lives lost\, support those still struggling\, and unite our com
 munity to take meaningful action. The overdose crisis has left a deep mark
  on families here in Foley and across Baldwin County.\nIt’s not just ind
 ividuals who are affected—it’s classrooms\, churches\, workplaces and 
 the communities we call home. At Big Fish Ministries\, we’ve seen firsth
 and how pain can isolate\, but also how healing can bring people together.
  In a time when so many are searching for hope\, we are reminded that our 
 lives are more connected than we often realize.\nWe all fiercely protect t
 hose we love—our children\, our spouses\, our friends. But what if we ex
 tended that same compassion and care to everyone impacted by addiction and
  loss? What if we saw each other as one big family with shared struggles\,
  united by hope?\nThis August 30\, let’s reimagine what it means to be a
  family—one that stands for grace and second chances. Every story told\,
  every candle lit\, and every voice lifted matters. We invite you to stand
  with us as we remember those we’ve lost and commit to building a future
  where fewer lives are cut short. Together\, we can help write a different
  story.\nSpecial Guest Speaker: Francis Holk-Jones\n\n---\n🌐 View origi
 nal event: https://businesshub.southbaldwinchamber.com/calendar/Details/ov
 erdose-drug-awareness-day-1888662
LOCATION:Foley Heritage Park\, 125 E. Laurel Ave\, Foley\,\, AL\, 36535\, 
 United States
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
